<title>USA: FirstFed says CEO retiring, names successor.</title>
<headline>FirstFed says CEO retiring, names successor.</headline>
<dateline>SANTA MONICA, Calif 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>FirstFed Financial Corp said Wednesday that Chief Executive William Mortensen is retiring January 1, and will be succeeded by Babette Heimbuch, the company's president and chief operating officer.</p>
<p>Mortensen, who has been the chief executive for the past 28 years, is to remain as chairman of the board of directors.</p>
<p>Heimbuch has been with the bank since 1982, joining the firm shortly before its conversion to a publicly held bank from a mutual savings and loan association.</p>
